    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Issues and Solutions\n\n**Issue 1: Missing named export in governance module**\n- The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only available in the default export\n- **Fix**: Added explicit named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`, and all the functions while maintaining the default export\n\n**Issue 2: Toxicity metric function signature mismatch**\n- The `toxicityMetric` function had signature `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but was being called by `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`\n- This caused the references array to be interpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs as toxic\n- **Fix**: Updated the function signature to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms)` to match the calling convention, with `references` as an ignored parameter\n\n**Test Results:**\n- All 8 test files passing \u2705\n- All 28 tests passing \u2705\n- No test files modified\n- All public exports preserved",
